course: dictionary
lesson: 5344
title: Your kidneys
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your kidneys are two bean-shaped organs in your lower back. An organ is a part of the body that does a special job. Your blood carries things around your body, and it also carries waste.
explain: Your kidneys clean your blood like a filter. They take out waste and extra water, and this leaves your body as urine, which is also called wee. The wee travels to your bladder until you go to the toilet.
explain: «Lilies are very poisonous to cats; even pollen licked off their fur can damage the kidneys.» Here kidneys are organs inside a body. Damage means they could be harmed and stop cleaning the blood well. Kidney has a second meaning too: the kidneys of an animal eaten as food, as in steak and kidney pie. Check the sentence: does your meaning make sense in it?
fact: Your kidneys are two bean-shaped organs in your lower back.
fact: Your kidneys clean your blood by removing waste and extra water.
fact: Waste and extra water leave the body as urine (wee), which passes to the bladder.
fact: People can live with one kidney, and kidney transplants can save lives.
fact: Drinking enough water helps your kidneys work well.
exercise: «Lilies can damage the kidneys of cats.» What do your kidneys do in your body? | They help you hear sounds | They make your bones strong | *They clean the blood by removing waste and extra water | They pump blood around your body
exercise: «Kidney beans» are named after their shape. Why are they called kidney beans? | *Because their shape is like a kidney | Because they grow inside animals | Because they clean the blood | Because they are cooked in pies
exercise: «People needing a new kidney often wait for years.» What is it called when a sick person gets a new kidney from a donor? | A kidney pie | A kidney lesson | A kidney bean | *A kidney transplant
test: «Raw or undercooked kidney beans contain a natural substance that makes people sick.» What should you do to make them safe to eat? | *Boil them properly until they are cooked | Eat them raw with salad | Leave them in the sun to dry
test: What do your kidneys make, which then travels to the bladder? | Tears | Blood | Bones | *Wee (urine)
exam: Which helps your kidneys work well? | Eating only sweets all day | Staying in bed all day | *Drinking enough water | Holding in your wee for days
